and the shutdown is also affecting  airport screeners who have to keep  working without pay Kris Van Cleave is  at Washington Dragons National Airport  tracking the potential impact on air  safety Kris everyone is paying attention  to this closely  well good morning absolutely you know  the TSA leadership remains very  concerned about a potential tipping  point moment when screeners will look  elsewhere to pay their bills because you  know today they got a pay stub with zero  dollars on it and that could really make  it a lot harder to staff checkpoints  like the one behind me here it is  important to note that the vast majority  of TSA officers have been on the job  throughout the shutdown working without  pay but there has been a modest increase  in the number of sick calls compared to  last year  if staffing becomes an issue the TSA  will reduce the number of screening  lanes that will result in longer lines  and the very real potential of missed  flights Miami International Airport is  prepared to close terminal G in the  afternoons starting this weekend to free  up TSA officers to work busier  checkpoints in part due to sick calls  FAA air traffic controllers rallied on  Capitol Hill yesterday calling for an  end of the shutdown they're also on the  job working without pay one controller  posted this picture on Twitter of her  pay stub showing zero dollars the NTSB  can investigate fatal crashes right now  because it's investigators have been  furloughed and they can only bring them  back if there is a reasonable likelihood  of a life threatening safety issue be  honest unbelievable Chris so aside from  the inconvenience of longer lines if TSA  screeners don't show up for work is it  still safe to fly well so far the vast  majority have shown up to work if they  stop showing up to work you won't be  able to go through security and you  won't be able to fly but right now there  there's no talk of safety issues air  traffic controllers are on the job TSA  screeners are on the job it's safe to  fly all right thank you Chris could I  just say when I was at the airport last  week passengers were thanking the TSA  screeners for being being there on the  job you might want to think about that  when you're flying that's right people  are there without pay working one yeah  absolutely that's exactly right
 

